cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "agent-convergence-scorer: behavioral convergence scoring for non-deterministic LLM agents"
abstract: >-
  agent-convergence-scorer is a behavioral evaluation tool that scores how
  similar N agent outputs are - exact-match rate, Jaccard token overlap,
  divergence point, and a composite 0-1 convergence score over any fan-out of
  agent runs. It judges agents by what they actually produce across repeated
  trials rather than by their configuration. Stdlib-only, zero runtime
  dependencies.
type: software
authors:
